{
  "$schema": "https://schema.agentcore.aws.dev/v1/agentcore.json",
  "name": "governed-agentic-companion",
  "version": 1,
  "managedBy": "CDK",
  "tags": {
    "project": "governed-agentic-companion"
  },
  "_comment": "OPTIONAL / LEGACY CLI REFERENCE. The DEPLOYABLE path for this kit is the Terraform stack at agentcore/terraform/ (see agentcore/README.md + docs/DEPLOY.md) — it provisions both runtimes, the native protocol_type=MCP gateway with an mcp_server target, Cognito, KB, memory, guardrail, and the interceptor. This file is kept only as a reference for teams who prefer the AgentCore CLI project shape; if you use it, copy to a gitignored agentcore.json and fill placeholders. Two runtimes: `orchestrator` (/invocations) and `mcp-runtime` (stateless /mcp, the gateway target). buildContextPath is the REPO ROOT so the single-source engine (agents/, governance/, knowledge/) is COPY-able directly.",
  "runtimes": [
    {
      "name": "orchestrator",
      "build": "Container",
      "type": "byo",
      "entrypoint": "agentcore/app/orchestrator/runtime_entrypoint.py",
      "codeLocation": "agentcore/app/orchestrator/",
      "dockerfile": "agentcore/app/orchestrator/Dockerfile",
      "buildContextPath": "..",
      "runtimeVersion": "PYTHON_3_12",
      "networkMode": "PUBLIC",
      "protocol": "HTTP",
      "_comment_authorizer": "Inbound auth. Set authorizerType CUSTOM_JWT + authorizerConfiguration.customJwtAuthorizer to require an IdP JWT. The platform validates the token (issuer, audience/allowed-clients, signature, expiry) at the edge BEFORE the request reaches the container, and does not forward it — so the example engine does no in-code token validation. discoveryUrl/allowedClients embed the IdP tenant, so they belong in the gitignored config. (Terraform: runtimes.tf sets this from the resolved auth_mode.)",
      "authorizerType_example": "CUSTOM_JWT",
      "authorizerConfiguration_example": {
        "customJwtAuthorizer": {
          "discoveryUrl": "https://<your-idp-issuer>/.well-known/openid-configuration",
          "allowedClients": ["<your-runtime-client-id>"]
        }
      },
      "_comment_envVars": "The engine reads the curated Tier-B overlay from S3: GAC_KB_OVERLAY=s3 + GAC_KB_BUCKET + GAC_KB_OVERLAY_KEY (the FULL object key, not a prefix) + GAC_AWS_REGION. Tier-A locked constraints stay image-only and the overlay cannot touch them. The Terraform stack (agentcore/terraform/locals.tf) is the authoritative source of this env contract; keep this example in sync with it.",
      "envVars_example": [
        { "name": "GAC_KB_OVERLAY", "value": "s3" },
        { "name": "GAC_KB_BUCKET", "value": "<your-kb-bucket-name>" },
        { "name": "GAC_KB_OVERLAY_KEY", "value": "kb/curated/overlay.json" },
        { "name": "GAC_AWS_REGION", "value": "<your-region>" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "mcp-runtime",
      "build": "Container",
      "type": "byo",
      "entrypoint": "agentcore/app/mcp_runtime/runtime_mcp_entrypoint.py",
      "codeLocation": "agentcore/app/mcp_runtime/",
      "dockerfile": "agentcore/app/mcp_runtime/Dockerfile",
      "buildContextPath": "..",
      "runtimeVersion": "PYTHON_3_12",
      "networkMode": "PUBLIC",
      "_comment_protocol": "MCP runtime serves the stateless streamable-HTTP MCP contract on port 8000 at /mcp. Deploy as protocol MCP; the platform health-checks port 8000. This is the upstream MCP server the Gateway's mcp_server target points at.",
      "protocol": "MCP",
      "envVars_example": [
        { "name": "GAC_KB_OVERLAY", "value": "s3" },
        { "name": "GAC_KB_BUCKET", "value": "<your-kb-bucket-name>" },
        { "name": "GAC_KB_OVERLAY_KEY", "value": "kb/curated/overlay.json" },
        { "name": "GAC_AWS_REGION", "value": "<your-region>" }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "_comment_gateways": "Provision a protocol_type=MCP Gateway with an mcp_server target whose endpoint is the mcp-runtime's /mcp invocations URL. Inbound = CUSTOM_JWT (the builder's IdP JWT, PKCE for the IDE path). Outbound to the runtime = OAuth M2M (a Cognito client_credentials grant + a resource-server scope, e.g. gac-engine/invoke) via an AgentCore Identity credential provider. The gateway target name (e.g. 'gac') namespaces its tools as gac___<tool>. The gateway's /mcp URL becomes GAC_GATEWAY_URL for the front doors. NOTE: agentcore/terraform/gateway.tf is the authoritative, deployable definition; this block is a reference only. See agentcore/README.md.",
  "agentCoreGateways_example": [
    {
      "name": "gac-gateway",
      "protocolType": "MCP",
      "authorizerType": "CUSTOM_JWT",
      "authorizerConfiguration": {
        "customJwtAuthorizer": {
          "discoveryUrl": "https://<your-idp-issuer>/.well-known/openid-configuration",
          "allowedClients": ["<your-frontdoor-client-id>"]
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "name": "gac",
          "type": "mcp_server",
          "runtimeRef": "mcp-runtime",
          "outboundAuth": {
            "type": "oauth-m2m",
            "credentialProviderRef": "gac-m2m"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "memories": [],
  "knowledgeBases": [],
  "credentials": [],
  "evaluators": [],
  "policyEngines": []
}
